@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About - Utkeern</PageTitle>

<section class="about-hero">
    <div class="about-hero-content">
        <h1>About Utkeern</h1>
        <p>A personal journey preserving the legacy of Indian heritage</p>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="content">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="about-narrative grid-2">
            <div class="about-image">
                <img src="images/About me page.webp" alt="Heritage preservation journey" />
            </div>
            <div class="about-text">
                <h2>Preserving Heritage, Sharing Knowledge</h2>
                <p>
                    Utkeern is a digital heritage initiative dedicated to promoting awareness, learning, and scholarly engagement with 
                    India's rich cultural heritage.
                    The platform has been developed as an educational resource for students, educators, researchers,
                    and heritage enthusiasts seeking reliable and accessible information on art, architecture, inscriptions,
                    archaeology, and cultural history.
                </p>
                <p>
                    The primary objective of Utkeern is to make valuable knowledge, documentation, field observations, 
                    and research materials easily available to present and future generations.
                    By bringing together diverse resources in one place, the platform aims to support learning, teaching, and independent research.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Special emphasis is placed on documenting and highlighting lesser-known aspects of Indian heritage that have received 
                    limited academic attention. Through carefully curated content and research-based documentation, Utkeern seeks to encourage 
                    greater scholarly interest in understudied monuments, 
                    inscriptions, traditions, and cultural landscapes.
                </p>
                <p>
                    By fostering awareness and facilitating access to quality information, Utkeern aspires to contribute to the preservation, appreciation, 
                    and deeper understanding of India's diverse heritage for generations to come.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<div class="heritage-divider"></div>

<section class="content alt">
    <div class="container-sm">
        <SectionHeader Title="Mission & Values" />

        <div class="grid-3">
            <ValueCard 
                Title="Preservation" 
                Description="Documenting and archiving heritage through high-quality visual and written content." />
            
            <ValueCard 
                Title="Education" 
                Description="Making heritage knowledge accessible to students and lifelong learners worldwide." />
            
            <ValueCard Title="Awareness"
                       Description="Fostering awareness of cultural heritage through research, education, and meaningful engagement with history and traditions." />
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<div class="heritage-divider"></div>

<section class="content">
    <div class="container-sm">
        <SectionHeader Title="The Creator" />

        <div class="creator-bio grid-2">
            <div class="bio-image">
                <img src="images/Profile.jpg" alt="Creator portrait" />
            </div>
            <div class="bio-content">
                <h3>Hello, I'm Dr. Nikita Ratore</h3>
                <p>
                    Assistant Professor in the Department of Palaeography, Epigraphy & Numismatics at the Indian Institute of Heritage,
                    Noida. My research focuses on temple art, architecture, and inscriptions, 
                    with particular emphasis on the Paramara dynasty of Western and South-Western Madhya Pradesh.
                </p>
                <div class="bio-highlights">
                    <ul>
                        <li>Specialist in Temple Art, Architecture, and Epigraphy</li>
                        <li>Proficient in Brahmi Script and Sanskrit</li>
                        <li>Published Researcher with National and International Academic Contributions</li>
                        <li>Sahapedia-UNESCO Fellow (2018)</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="bio-cta">
                    <a href="mailto:nikks14.1@gmail.com" class="btn btn-primary">Get in Touch</a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

